Subject: [PATCH] emote: wire reactive waveform face to live Gemini audio levels

Patch 0031 built the reactive waveform on a pluggable amplitude source, self-
contained on synthetic amplitude. This wires the LIVE source: cap_gemini_live's
audio level getters → the waveform's LISTENING/SPEAKING bars.

The glue lives in the app_claw layer (the only place that knows both APIs), so
cap_gemini_live stays display-agnostic and the emote component stays voice-
agnostic. New app_claw_face_bridge.{c,h}:
  - gl_face_amp(state): LISTENING → cap_gemini_live_get_mic_level(),
    SPEAKING → cap_gemini_live_get_output_level() (both float 0.0..1.0),
    scaled per-stream to 0..1000 for emote_face_amp_cb_t.
  - app_claw_face_bridge_register(): emote_face_set_amplitude_source(gl_face_amp).
Registered from app_claw_ui_start() right after emote_start().

NORMALIZATION (tune after hardware test): ES7210 in-gain=30 → typical speech mic
RMS ~2000-6000 raw → ~0.06..0.18 after the getter's /32768, so mic is scaled
×6.0. Gemini TTS output reads much hotter, scaled ×1.6. The render task's lerp
provides fast-attack/slow-decay smoothing. If speech reads flat/dead or clips on
the panel, adjust FACE_MIC_GAIN / FACE_OUT_GAIN (or ask voice-eng to bump the
ADC in-gain) and reship.

Double-gated: CONFIG_APP_CLAW_ENABLE_EMOTE (bridge compiled) AND
CONFIG_APP_CLAW_CAP_GEMINI_LIVE (live path); the latter off → a no-op stub, so
the waveform still runs on synthetic amplitude via the `face` CLI (patch 0031).
The two synthetic paths stay independent: the `face` CLI drives the display
directly; cap_gemini_live_set_synthetic_levels() is voice-eng's audio-path test.

Files (applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh apply_reactive_waveform_audio_bridge_patch;
bridge .c/.h vendored under firmware/emote/, copied in like 0031's waveform.c):
  + components/common/app_claw/app_claw_face_bridge.c   (new)
  + components/common/app_claw/app_claw_face_bridge.h   (new)
  ~ components/common/app_claw/app_claw.c               (include + register call)
  ~ components/common/app_claw/CMakeLists.txt           (add .c, emote-gated)

ABI note: depends on cap_gemini_live's FLOAT getters (get_mic_level /
get_output_level, 0.0..1.0) — the version actually staged. (An earlier uint16
*_rms variant was discussed but not shipped.)
